    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey my 2018 honda civic is making this really loud squealing noise whenever i step on the gas to accelerate. i think it might be the serpentine belt? can you explain how that belt actually works and why it would make that kind of noise if it's worn out?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The serpentine belt is a long, ribbed belt that drives various accessories like the alternator, power steering pump, and A/C compressor using pulleys on the engine. It works by transmitting rotational power from the engine's crankshaft to these components through friction. A squealing noise usually indicates the belt is slipping, often because it is too loose, worn out, or the pulleys are misaligned.",
