      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, things other than just belt material wear can cause slipping. A worn or failing tensioner pulley won't apply the necessary constant pressure across the belt, causing it to slip under load. Additionally, a dirty or glazed pulley surface, or even corrosion on the pulleys, can prevent the belt from gripping properly, leading to that loud squeal during acceleration.",
